  "note": "Triennial election of the county council, 1927: nominations received by Thomas E. Reid, secretary, 26 April 1927; the only poll was in Portadown, 26 May 1927. No party labels are printed for the unopposed members in the nominations or the list of the new council, so none are given. Polled 26 May 1927, declared 27 May. Hall and Rock were the official Unionist candidates, Locke and Rowlett \"also Unionists\"; the sitting member Robert Anderson withdrew. 3,090 votes recorded (68 per cent of the electorate), 32 spoilt."
